WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.770
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.673
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.575 line:0%
Well, guys, yesterday,
The White House

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.677 line:0%
had a press briefing,
and they announced that

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:15.114 line:0%
they reached out to North Korea
to restart nuclear talks

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:16.816 line:0%
but had not heard back.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.552
At first, I thought the reason
for the lack of response

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.221
might be that Kim Jong-Un
uses a fax machine,

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:25.658
but then I remembered Biden
does, too, so...

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:28.894
Well, hours after
The White House said

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:31.163
it hadn't received
a response from North Korea,

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:33.299
Kim Jong-Un's sister
made a statement.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.467
Listen to this.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.836 line:0%
-This new warning to
the Biden administration.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.438 line:0%
She says...

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.780
-Ooh!

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.885
-Okay!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.220
-Okay.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.322
Yeah, nice try, North Korea,
but we're America.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.625
We haven't slept well
for the past five years, so...

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.393
Seriously,
only four years without sleep

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:02.962
sounds like a bargain.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.263
Also, I like that Kim Jong-Un

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:06.366
had his sister deliver
the message.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.634
It's like North Korea's
version of,

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.068
"I heard a noise in America.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:12.305
Go check it out."

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.673
Oh, and here's some big news.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.609 line:0%
According to U.S. intelligence,
Russia and Iran

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:20.212 line:0%
tried to interfere with
the 2020 election.

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:25.118
Biden's like, "Well, whatever
you did, thanks, fellas."

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.020
Yeah.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.687
This is pretty rough news
for Trump.

00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:30.022
It's like losing
in Little League

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:33.526
and then finding out
your dad bribed the ump.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:37.162
Right now, Putin and
the ayatollah are on a couch

00:01:37.162 --> 00:01:38.831
like a Nora Ephron movie.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.533
[ Russian accent ]
We met hacking the election.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.067
He wanted to hack ballots.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.536
I wanted to hack Twitter.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.773 line:0%
And we've been together
ever since.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:52.946
Well, some business news here.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.480
I saw that Mountain Dew
is releasing

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.617
a new sugar-free soda called
Frost Bite Zero Sugar.

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.386
Here's a photo.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.888
Yeah, something tells me that
if you're drinking

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:04.357
a neon-blue drink called
Frost Bite,

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:08.728
you're not that worried about
the sugar content.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.996
Meanwhile, I saw that
Heinz just launched

00:02:10.996 --> 00:02:13.699
three new
combo condiments called

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:18.404
Hanch, Wasabioli, and Tarchup.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.305
-Yes!

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:22.608
-When asked how they came
up with these, Heinz was like,

00:02:22.608 --> 00:02:26.379
"We got draked --
drunk and baked."

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.018
I'm actually trying to be
a little healthier,

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:36.455
so I'm waiting for Tarchup Zero.

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:38.958
That's right -- there are
three new combo condiments.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.794
There's Tarchup, which is
tartar sauce and ketchup,

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.730
Hanch, which is
hot sauce and ranch,

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.234
and Wasabioli,
which is wasabi and aioli.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.503
They're funny names,
but some of the other combos

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.038
they tried
didn't really work out.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.673
For example,
they tried combining

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:56.109
balsamic and hot sauce
and got...

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.017
Then they combined
oil, aioli, and mayo and got...

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:10.022
And, finally, they combined
beef gravy, Italian dressing,

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:13.426
and Greek yogurt in a wok
with barbecue sauce and got...

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.599
I mean, that's...

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.169
This is interesting.

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:26.905
A new study found that almost
80% of Manhattan office workers

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:30.042
will not return to
their workplace full time

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.977
once their office reopens.

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:35.748
Yep, 80% are happy that they
won't return to their workplace,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:39.818
while the other 20% are parents.

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:43.089
"I'll be back in 15 hours.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.857
You guys know how to tuck
yourselves in, right?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.159
Cool. See ya."

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:49.762
Yeah, bosses are already trying
to get people to come back.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.829
They're like, "Come on.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:53.733
There's free Hanch
in the kitchen."

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.969
It sort of makes sense.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:59.171
It's basically, "Do I want
my three-bedroom office

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:00.373
with a private bathroom

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.374
or do I want to share a cubicle
with Frank,

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:05.912
the guy in the office
who burns microwave popcorn?"

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.982
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.382
There's someone here
that does that.

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:11.751
I forget who it is.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.586
I'll find out.
I always smell it.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.920
Is that you, Quest?
-Yeah.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.189
-I go, "Come on, man.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.757
If you're gonna do it,
just make -- Just stop it.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.725
You know,
I know you'll waste 10 kernels.

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:20.727
Just don't --"

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.995
"I got to push all the way.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:24.097
Got to get
all those kernels popped."

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.566
You ruined it, burned it, and
the whole office smells like it.

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:30.369
-2 minutes and 37 seconds.
I got it to a science.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:31.704
-No way, man. No, no.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:35.074
I'm sensor pop all the way, man.
-Sensor pop?

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.076
-Yeah, man.
You got to do it by the sensors.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.678
You type "popcorn sensor,"
and it shuts off automatically.

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:42.615
-It does?
-Yeah.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.850
-I got to try that.
-It totally works.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.053
You know how they do it?
-How do they do it?

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:50.223
-What do you think? Any guesses?

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:54.460
-Um, I would guess that it's,
like -- It's an audio thing.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.829
Like, it's -- Once, you know --

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.164
But you're talking
microwave oven, right?

00:04:58.164 --> 00:04:59.332
-Correct.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:02.234
-Once the microwave,
like, no longer hears

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:06.672
the popping sound or, you know,
once the pops are a certain,

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:10.042
you know, distance apart
or amount of time apart,

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.944
then it shuts down.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.480
-Because you think it slows --
the popping slows down to --

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.882
-I know the popping slows down
as the popcorn --

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.518
That's -- Here's what we know.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:21.787
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.856
When you cook some popcorn...
-Uh-huh.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.125
-...the closer it is
to being completely done,

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:28.261
the less it's gonna pop,
because, you know,

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.696
the kernels have already popped.

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:31.763
But there may be some strays,
you know.

00:05:31.763 --> 00:05:33.766
-You got a couple strays there,
which totally

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.235
debunks your theory, so, no,
you're wrong, unfortunately.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:39.572
-Uh, I don't know. Okay.
How's it work?

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:42.408
-Uh, uh...steam.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.544
-Ah!
-There you go, everybody.

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:48.480
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.215
-And now back to the show.

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:54.286
[ Bell dings ]
-Speaking of...

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:55.787
Speaking of working from home,

00:05:55.787 --> 00:05:57.756
there's a new app
for Zoom users.

00:05:57.756 --> 00:05:58.890
Check this out.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.526
-The Zoom Escaper app.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:03.629
It allows Zoom users
to sabotage their own calls

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.365
with sound effects,
like a crying baby.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:09.569
You can also make it seem as if
you have a bad connection.

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:13.572
-Yeah. That's right -- an app
that will make it seem like

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:15.174
your Zoom has
technical difficulties.

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:18.778
So, basically,
these guys invented Zoom.

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:23.082
And, finally, some news for
Mega Millions players.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:24.116
Watch this.

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.717 line:0%
-An unclaimed
Mega Millions ticket

00:06:25.717 --> 00:06:27.887 line:0%
purchased last year
is set to expire tomorrow.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.755 line:0%
The winning ticket was
bought in Rhode Island

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.857 line:0%
on St. Patrick's Day 2020.

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:34.826 line:0%
It's worth $1 million,
and the rightful owner

00:06:34.826 --> 00:06:37.964 line:0%
has less than 24 hours
to accept the lump sum.

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:41.033
-You know last March, a guy left
the ticket in his office

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.534
next to a half-eaten sandwich,
thinking,

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:43.569
"I'll take care of
this tomorrow."

